50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are A: Campus Path Network, B: Media Production Center, C: Central Study Commons, and D: Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade. I lean toward C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Yumi,,C is perfect! It provides the general-purpose rooms I found are so desperately needed.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,George,,"D would help the technicians with their manual routines, but C seems less demanding on the grounds staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"A is exposed to weather, and D involves mechanical plant and potentially hazardous materials. C is the most user-friendly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"B lacks a renewal reserve for its kit, and D's costs are likely to exceed the budget. C is the most rational choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, would the conversion for the Study Commons be too disruptive to the schedule?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, do you think the Study Commons would get those high post-occupancy ratings?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,George,,"As long as it's an internal conversion, it avoids the weather risks Shizue mentioned.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, yes, because it's a shared resource bookable by any department.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It avoids the mechanical price hikes of D and the weather volatility of A.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am quite happy with C. It seems the safest and most helpful.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for C! It's exactly what the students need.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,George,,I can support C. It doesn't add to the grounds staff's burden.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. C avoids the pitfalls of the older blocks' partitions if handled correctly.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logically, C has the fewest financial and operational red flags.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
